 "observations": [
  "The field's frame, checked against the defining papers: the received reading holds that the denial is of a systematic, formal or complete art, with predecessors in practice (SEP Ancient Logic: 'logic as a fully systematic discipline begins with Aristotle, who systematized much of the logical inquiry of his predecessors'; SEP Aristotle's Logic: 'the earliest formal study of logic'); the archive's papers state that reading first and at full strength (#1570 §0A.2; #1575 §I.3; #1576 §1; #1603 §1) and argue against it at the sentence's own words.",
  "The archive is not uniform across dates: #1570 (2026-08-29) holds practice-versus-art to be 'Aristotle's own frame, in this passage'; #1603 (2026-09-08) holds the defender's contrast of discipline and untheorized practice 'not on the page'. Carried as contested in the pool, both, with dates; not a defect.",
  "The Socrates placement is graded in the archive itself: #1574 §9 does not establish Socrates inside the 'we'; #1603 §5 argues inclusion 'controversially' and claims it as asserted, not demonstrated; Appendix P's joints withhold the maker question; #1576 §9.4 states the single-maker reading as a hypothesis whose result is only that 'two is not established by these passages'.",
  "The hop is dominated by #1684 (the prediction index cites most of the archive): 787 of 871 hop candidates come through it alone. Those were screened by string, not read (see not_admitted).",
  "#123 is not a string candidate and was reached only by the hop; it was read at its defining sections and not admitted (reason recorded)."
